  "EditorMetadata": {
    "Description": "P1b (Hill-attack -\u003E Blueprints migration), tree-INTEGRATION track (architect Q#9-A): the integrated twin of HillAssault2_CalculateSegments -- SAME SegmentMath.TotalSlots logic (GetParameter StartX/StartY/EndX/EndY/TankSpacing -\u003E curated SegmentMath.TotalSlots pure FunctionCall), but leaves its native WorkingState EMPTY and converses over the standalone entity-scoped HillAttackSharedState struct via GetShared/SetShared(VariableId=\u0022state\u0022), so it can be composed alongside sibling integrated nodes in a real commander .btree.json without each node owning a colliding private WorkingState (per-blueprint WorkingState types never match byte-for-byte across distinct generated _Bp\u002BWorkingState structs). Graph: EventEntry -\u003E SetShared(\u0022state\u0022) -\u003E Return(Success), where SetShared.Value is fed by a chain of pure HillAttackSharedStateOps.With* FunctionCalls seeded from GetShared(\u0022state\u0022).Value: WithTotalSlots(SegmentMath.TotalSlots(...)) -\u003E WithBurnedSlotsMask((ushort)0) -\u003E WithWaveUsedSlotsMask((ushort)0) -\u003E WithBaselineReservedMask((ushort)0) -\u003E WithCachedEqsRequestId(-1L) -\u003E WithCachedTargetGroupHandle(-1) -\u003E WithEqsRequestTime(0f) -\u003E WithCurrentWave(0). Does not zero ActiveRunners -- mirrors the oracle/isolated-twin\u0027s CalculateSegments, which does not touch the runner tracker either. Does not modify the C# oracle, the isolated twin (HillAssault2_CalculateSegments.bp.json), or the compiler.",
    "Category": null,
    "Recipe": null
  }
